    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n971" root="اقط" body-key="A">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقَطَهُ</span></b> , aor 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَقِطَ</span></b>  (S, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقْطٌ</span>, (S,) <i>He
made it</i> (namely food) <i>with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقِط</span> q. v. infrà.
(S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, (aor. and inf. n. as above, TA,)
<i>He fed him with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقِط</span>: (A'Obeyd, K:) like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَنَهُ</span>
from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَنٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَأَهُ</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِبَأٌ</span> Lh mentions the
verb in this sense as used without its being made
transitive. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقِطَ</span> in the CK is a mistake
for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آقَطَ</span> q. v.]

